From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:37:19 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: the updater on Windows

Off macOS Settings only showed the version. On Windows Meridian now updates
itself as on the Mac: it asks GitHub for the latest release a little after
it starts and then daily, downloads that release's installer
(Meridian-<version>-win-<arch>-setup.exe), and checks it against the
checksums the Windows build publishes beside it (SHA256SUMS-win.txt), which
it trusts only under Meridian's release key, the same one as the Mac's.
"Restart to update" quits and lets a small script run the installer once
Meridian is gone, then open it again. Only a copy an installer put there
updates itself; a build in out/ doesn't.

The release parsing is one function for both systems with the names each
looks for; the Mac's are what they were.

Linux keeps the stub.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
